Subject: [PATCH] Point functional Bolt URLs at boltapp.com (plugin 2.10.0)

Port of the bolt-magento2 domain migration (BoltApp/bolt-magento2 #1973) onto
the Magento 1 plugin's 2.10.0 release tag.

Rewrites the Bolt service hosts the plugin calls at runtime -- api, connect and
merchant, production and sandbox -- from bolt.com to boltapp.com. All of them
live in Helper/UrlTrait.php; Block/Checkout/Boltpay.php builds connect.js and
track.js from those constants, and the API, GraphQL and configuration helpers
go through getApiUrl() / getBoltMerchantUrl(). The admin help text in
etc/system.xml that names merchant.bolt.com/settings moves with them.

Helper/UrlTrait.php::validateCustomUrl is widened to bolt(app)?\.(me|com) so a
merchant-supplied custom sandbox URL on boltapp.com is not silently rejected and
replaced with the default. The existing bolt.com and bolt.me hosts stay accepted.

Left alone on purpose: the www.bolt.com copyright headers, the dev@bolt.com
contact address, the na@bolt.com Apple Pay prefill sentinel (a value match, not
a host), docs.bolt.com and support.bolt.com help links (docs.boltapp.com does
not resolve), and CHANGELOG.md.

The unit tests that assert the old hosts are updated in the same patch, so the
suite stays green.

Apply from the plugin root (the directory that holds app/ and js/):

    git apply bolt-magento1-2.10.0-boltapp-domains.patch
    # or, without git:
    patch -p1 < bolt-magento1-2.10.0-boltapp-domains.patch

---
